\begin_layout Title
Statistical Analysis (Hypothesis Testing) of Binary Data (Comparing Two Classifications)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Introduction
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
I will be performing a hypothesis test on binary data.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The data being analyzed is patent data relating to a specific type of rejection from the US Patent and Trademark Office.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
I will be compare two classes to see if their rejection rates vary statistically.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Hypothesis
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Ho:
 The null hypothesis is that there is no significant difference in Alice rejection rates between class 705 and class 706.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Ha:
 The alternate hypothesis is that there is a significant difference in Alice rejection rates between class 705 and class 706.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Data
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Data was collected through the USPTO API.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Method
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
I will first look at the percent of Alice rejections for each class.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Next I will create a 2x2 matrix using the crosstab function in pandas.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
I will then feed that matrix into the scipy fisher_exact test which handles the statistical analysis of proportions.
\end_layout

